@backend_HostAddress = http://localhost:5009

### Sign in as the seeded development author.
# @name login
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "author@example.com", "password": "ChangeMe!Dev123" }

###
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refreshToken}}

### Register a new author.
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Someone New", "email": "new@example.com", "password": "a long enough password" }

### Sign in with Google. The frontend obtains idToken from Google Identity Services;
### this needs Authentication:Google:ClientId to be configured.
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/auth/oauth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{ "idToken": "<google-id-token>" }

### Add Google to the signed-in account.
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/auth/oauth/google/link
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{ "idToken": "<google-id-token>" }

### Who am I, and how can this account sign in?
GET {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Trade the refresh token for a new pair. The old one is spent.
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### Sign out this session.
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### Public feed: published posts only.
GET {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/posts
Accept: application/json

### Authoring feed: your own posts, drafts included. 401 without a token.
GET {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/admin/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Only your drafts.
GET {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/admin/posts?isDraft=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Create a draft. It is filed under whoever the token identifies.
# @name createPost
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/admin/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{ "title": "A post written over HTTP", "summary": "Optional.", "body": "The body." }

### Publish it.
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/admin/posts/{{createPost.response.body.id}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Someone else's post: 403.
POST {{backend_HostAddress}}/api/admin/posts/4/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
